        <mxCell id="kUmSnzWs2xmoCplQeJRa-81" parent="kUmSnzWs2xmoCplQeJRa-80" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=18;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;x means External Input.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;We make it immutable so that we have a consistent x -to - state history&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;if we want to make a new state, we must create it from an x&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;if we modify x, that does not change the &#39;original x&#39; a state was based off on&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;i.e no in-place modification of x.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Since Threads are mutable, we take a snapshot of them, so there is no history error or trace errors&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="460" x="163" y="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
